      "why": "1 result/cycle is the only way to plausibly hit >=50 MSPS with a tight 2^-20 error budget. Pipelined is the area-cheapest 1/cycle family (no k/m multiplier chains), so it should dominate the min-luts_plus_ffs corner that the selection rule picks. W=18..24 and N=14..22 span the accuracy trade-off (accuracy_bits ~ N + guard terms) so the front from just-meets-error up to comfortable margin is covered; angle/frac guards kept small to hold area down."
